      "id": "reported-speech",
      "title": "Reported Speech",
      "icon": "💬",
      "description": "Someone says something. Later you tell a third person what they said. You are not quoting, you are reporting.",
      "rules": [
        "Pronouns change: I → he/she, we → they, you → I/he/she/they, my → his/her.",
        "Tense goes one step back: am/is → was, are → were, will → would, can → could, may → might, must → had to, have/has → had.",
        "Time words change: now → then, today → that day, tomorrow → the next day, yesterday → the day before, last week → the week before, next month → the following month.",
        "Place words change: here → there, this → that, these → those.",
        "Reporting verb: said → said that, said to → told, asked → asked, ordered → ordered, requested → requested, warned → warned."
      ],
      "cheatCodes": [
        "Says = no change. Said = one step back.",
        "Universal truths, habits, proverbs → tense does NOT change.",
        "Wh-question → asked + wh-word + subject + verb. No question mark in indirect.",
        "Yes/No question → asked if/whether + subject + verb.",
        "Order → told/ordered + object + to + verb. Negative → told + object + not to + verb.",
        "Exclamation → exclaimed with joy/sorrow + that...",
        "Let's → suggested that they should..."
      ],
      "questions": [
        {"q":"Susan said, \"I met your sister last week.\"","options":["Susan said that I met your sister last week.","Susan said that I had met your sister last week.","Susan said that he had met my sister that week.","Susan said that he had met my sister the week before."],"answer":3,"explanation":"met → had met, your → my, last week → the week before."},
        {"q":"Ivor said, \"You are not listening to me.\"","options":["Ivor said that you are not listening to her.","Ivor said that you were not listening to her.","Ivor said that I was not listening to her.","Ivor said I had not been listening to her."],"answer":2,"explanation":"are → were, you → I, me → her."},
        {"q":"Bee Lee said, \"I am very happy today because my father has given me a car.\" (A month later.)","options":["Bee Lee said that he was very happy that day because his father has given him a car.","Bee Lee said that he was very happy that day because his father had given him a car.","Bee Lee said that he is very happy today because his father has given him a car.","Bee Lee said that he was very happy today because his father has given him a car."],"answer":1,"explanation":"am → was, today → that day, has given → had given."},
        {"q":"The headmistress says, \"The young people of today are tomorrow's leaders.\"","options":["The headmistress says that the young people of today are tomorrow's leaders.","The headmistress says that the young people of that day are the next day's leaders.","The headmistress said that the young people of that day are the next day's leaders.","The headmistress said that the young people of yesterday are today's leaders."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Says (present) → no tense change."},
        {"q":"The children said, \"We will build a sand-castle ourselves.\"","options":["The children said that they would build a sand-castle themselves.","The children said that they will build a sand-castle ourselves.","The children said that we would build a sand-castle ourselves.","The children said that we will build a sand-castle themselves."],"answer":0,"explanation":"will → would, we → they, ourselves → themselves."},
        {"q":"He said, \"I am looking at the diagram.\"","options":["He said that I am looking at the diagram.","He said that I was looking at the diagram.","He says that he was looking at the diagram.","He said that he was looking at the diagram."],"answer":3,"explanation":"am → was, I → he."},
        {"q":"Steven said, \"I don't have any money to pay for this ticket.\"","options":["Steven said that he don't have any money to pay for this ticket.","Steven said that he doesn't have any money to pay for that ticket.","Steven said that he didn't have any money to pay for that ticket.","Steven said that he hadn't had any money to pay for that ticket."],"answer":2,"explanation":"don't → didn't, this → that."},
        {"q":"Jill said, \"Jack must give his answer to me.\"","options":["Jill said that Jack must give her answer to him.","Jill said that Jack had to give his answer to her.","Jill said that Jack had to give his answer to me.","Jill said that Jack must give his answer to me."],"answer":1,"explanation":"must → had to, me → her."},
        {"q":"She said, \"I have been sewing from morning until now.\" (Next day.)","options":["She said that she had been sewing from morning until then.","She said that she has been sewing from morning until then.","She said that she had been sewing from morning until now.","She said that she has been sewing from morning until now."],"answer":0,"explanation":"have been → had been, now → then."},
        {"q":"Carl said, \"You may meet them next month.\"","options":["Carl said that you may meet them next month.","Carl said that I may meet them next month.","Carl said that I might meet them the following month.","Carl said that I may meet them the following month."],"answer":2,"explanation":"may → might, next month → the following month."},
        {"q":"Peter told his brother, \"Don't shake the table while I am writing!\"","options":["Peter told his brother not to shake the table while he was writing.","Peter told his brother don't shake the table while he was writing.","Peter told his brother to not shake the table while I am writing.","Peter told his brother that he should not shake the table."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Negative order → told + object + not to + verb. am writing → was writing."},
        {"q":"She told us, \"Please bring your own plates and spoons.\"","options":["She told us that please bring our own plates and spoons.","She requested us to bring our own plates and spoons.","She requested us bring our own plates and spoons.","She said us to bring our own plates and spoons."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Request → requested + object + to + verb."},
        {"q":"The officer ordered his men, \"Return to the ship immediately!\"","options":["The officer ordered his men return to the ship immediately.","The officer ordered his men to return to the ship immediately.","The officer ordered his men that they return to the ship immediately.","The officer ordered his men returning to the ship immediately."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Order → ordered + object + to + verb."},
        {"q":"David told his brother, \"Go to that drawer and bring me the scissors.\"","options":["David told his brother go to that drawer and bring him the scissors.","David told his brother to go to that drawer and bring him the scissors.","David told his brother that go to that drawer and bring me the scissors.","David told his brother to go to this drawer and bring me the scissors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Order → told + object + to + verb. that → this (from listener's view)."},
        {"q":"The storyteller told the children, \"The prince and princess lived happily ever after.\"","options":["The storyteller told the children that the prince and princess lived happily ever after.","The storyteller told the children that the prince and princess had lived happily ever after.","The storyteller told the children the prince and princess lived happily ever after.","The storyteller told the children that the prince and princess have lived happily ever after."],"answer":1,"explanation":"lived → had lived (past → past perfect)."},
        {"q":"The conductor said to the passengers, \"Don't push!\"","options":["The conductor told the passengers not to push.","The conductor told the passengers don't push.","The conductor said the passengers not push.","The conductor told the passengers to not pushing."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Negative command → told + object + not to + verb."},
        {"q":"He told his friend, \"I'm sorry, but I can't join you for lunch.\"","options":["He told his friend that he is sorry but he can't join him for lunch.","He told his friend that he was sorry but he couldn't join him for lunch.","He told his friend I am sorry but I can't join you for lunch.","He told his friend that he was sorry but he can't join him for lunch."],"answer":1,"explanation":"am → was, can't → couldn't, you → him."},
        {"q":"Miss Lam told the pupils, \"Do the exercises from pages sixty to sixty-two.\"","options":["Miss Lam told the pupils do the exercises from pages sixty to sixty-two.","Miss Lam told the pupils to do the exercises from pages sixty to sixty-two.","Miss Lam told the pupils that they do the exercises from pages sixty to sixty-two.","Miss Lam told the pupils doing the exercises from pages sixty to sixty-two."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Command → told + object + to + verb."},
        {"q":"The personnel officer asked, \"Do you know how to operate a computer?\"","options":["The personnel officer asked if I knew how to operate a computer.","The personnel officer asked do I know how to operate a computer.","The personnel officer asked that I knew how to operate a computer.","The personnel officer asked if I know how to operate a computer."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Yes/No question → asked if + subject + verb. know → knew."},
        {"q":"The elder sister asked, \"Are you mad at me?\"","options":["The elder sister asked are you mad at me.","The elder sister asked if I was mad at her.","The elder sister asked that I was mad at her.","The elder sister asked if you were mad at me."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Yes/No question → if + I + was + mad at her."},
        {"q":"The rich man said to the waitress, \"Keep the change.\"","options":["The rich man told the waitress to keep the change.","The rich man told the waitress keep the change.","The rich man said the waitress to keep the change.","The rich man told the waitress that keep the change."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Command → told + object + to + verb."},
        {"q":"I said to myself, \"I will definitely beat him in the next event.\"","options":["I told myself that I will definitely beat him in the next event.","I told myself that I would definitely beat him in the next event.","I told myself that I would definitely beat him in the following event.","I said to myself that I will definitely beat him in the next event."],"answer":1,"explanation":"will → would. 'next event' can stay or become 'following event' — best choice is B."},
        {"q":"He said, \"I found the money in the garden yesterday.\"","options":["He said that he found the money in the garden yesterday.","He said that he had found the money in the garden the day before.","He said that I had found the money in the garden yesterday.","He said that he has found the money in the garden the day before."],"answer":1,"explanation":"found → had found, yesterday → the day before."},
        {"q":"The teacher explained to us, \"The moon takes 28 days to go around the earth.\"","options":["The teacher explained that the moon took 28 days to go around the earth.","The teacher explained that the moon takes 28 days to go around the earth.","The teacher explained that the moon has taken 28 days to go around the earth.","The teacher explained that the moon had taken 28 days to go around the earth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Universal truth → tense does NOT change."},
        {"q":"Dad warned us, \"Don't touch the fresh paint!\"","options":["Dad warned us to not touch the fresh paint.","Dad warned us not to touch the fresh paint.","Dad warned us that don't touch the fresh paint.","Dad warned us don't touch the fresh paint."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Warning → warned + object + not to + verb."}
      ]
